   "subject": "Rstudio-server and shiny-server on same server, same port",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><div>Hi,<br><br></div>I was wondering :<br>Is it possible to have both rstudio-server and shiny-server listening to the same port ?<br><br></div>The perfect solution would be to be able to define rstudio-server config inside the shiny-server configuration, ie. allowing to put different server_name to each &quot;application&quot; (shiny app, rstudio session etc.).<br>\r\n\r\n<br></div>Any idea ?<br><br></div>Thanks,<br><br>Robin<br clear=\"all\"><div><div><div><div><div><br>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>Robin Cura<br></div>Doctorant à l&#39;<a href=\"http://www.parisgeo.cnrs.fr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.parisgeo.cnrs.fr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405415139000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0DTkPpmsePnXArsEnBLoAT\">UMR Géographie-cités</a><br>\r\n\r\n</div><a href=\"http://www.hesam.fr/pnm/labexdynamite/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.hesam.fr/pnm/labexdynamite/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405415139000&amp;usg=AOvVaw19tu67UdUAZs6Zd9YnzA6e\">LabEx DynamiTe</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://www.univ-paris1.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.univ-paris1.fr/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405415139000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3IxcXGIcJcAsjnTJlHqAJj\">Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne</a><br></div>\r\n</div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
